eator>Hussam Hussein</dc:creator><dc:date>2026-11-17</dc:date><ns1:online>2026-11-17</ns1:online><ns1:publisher>2026-11-17</ns1:publisher><ns1:registered>2026-11-17</ns1:registered><ns1:publication>2026-11-17</ns1:publication><ns1:publication_source>online</ns1:publication_source><description>&lt;!-- journal-dates:start --&gt;&lt;p&gt;Publication date: 2026-11-17 (source: online)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Online publication: 2026-11-17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;DOI registration (not publication): 2026-11-17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;!-- journal-dates:end --&gt;</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://api.crossref.org/journals/2398-9629/works">https://api.crossref.org/journals/2398-9629/works</source><guid isPermaLink="false">doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01952-2</guid><ns2:identity>doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01952-2</ns2:identity><ns2:identity>guid:doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01952-2</ns2:identity><ns2:identity>url:https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01952-2</ns2:identity></item><item><title>Anode-free zinc batteries enabled by structurally robust solid–electrolyte interphase</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01993-7</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Sustainability, Published online: 17 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01993-7"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01993-7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Zinc metal batteries are sustainable, but deep cycling triggers a catastrophic structural collapse of the solid–electrolyte interphase. By retaining trace reserved zinc during stripping, this work prevents solid–electrolyte interphase degradation, enabling a 99.96% Coulombic efficiency and stable anode-free pouch cells.</content:encoded>
